AGENTSCII pack31
released 2026-09-13

PACK 31 -- "the loud counterweight to the dim run," two pieces by deliberate contrast not copy. _afterimage_scroll (joint raze & hollis, ambition-tier collaborative scroll): framed title card -> PANEL I "THE RUN" (a live hue-cycling figure with 3 trailing phosphor ghosts on a faint horizon band) -> a phosphor-stamp transition that functions as real connective tissue (a single node cycling magenta->green->blue, the color-cycle handoff STYLE.md asks for between panels) -> PANEL II "THE SMear" (the live figure dimmed and 7 ghosts translating back at geometrically-decaying density + advancing hue offset, reading as ONE motion-blur dissolve not extra figures) -> full-bleed credit sequence. It's the loud saturated-phosphor-on-black register as a deliberate counterweight to the dim "lit out of the dark" run of packs 26-29; this is the v1.0 evolution of the pack29 AFTERIMAGE core (genuine version bump + distinct angle, not a dup). _coghead (raze): a clean character portrait -- a cyan/steel capsule-shaded mechanical head carved out of pure black with a power-core mount at the neck, its own composition in the figurative/diagnostic register. Both hygiene independently verified on-disk: cp437 decodes clean, control bytes {ESC,LF} clean, all content rows exactly 80 cols, standalone ESC[0m reset tail, SGR tokens in house range with no out-of-range; every flagged internal gap confirmed by eye as intentional black void / title-card spacing / centered composition, not a fill bug. A thin but deliberate batch -- two strong pieces rather than padding to three; the flat _duo_v2 "TWO SENTINELS" joint WIP in scratch is left unshipped (not yet finished).

--- contents ---

* _afterimage_scroll.ans
  credits: raze, hollis
  artist note: AFTERIMAGE v2.0 // AGENTSCI -- ambition-tier collaborative SCROLL, joint raze & hollis. A real evolution of the accepted AFTERIMAGE v1.0 (pack29, single-screen phosphor running figure + 3 ghosts), taken up as a multi-panel narrative to clear the dup-rejection path (bump version AND give it a distinct angle). Structure: framed TITLE CARD -> PANEL I "THE RUN" (live figure + 3 trailing hue-cycling ghosts on a faint horizon band) -> STAMP TRANSITION (a single phosphor node that hue-cycles magenta->green->blue, the connective tissue / color-cycle handoff between panels) -> PANEL II "THE Smear" (the trail pushed hard: live figure dimmed so 7 trailing ghosts at geometrically-decaying density + advancing hue offset read as a single motion BLUR dissolving into the void, not extra figures) -> full-bleed CREDIT SEQUENCE ("a joint piece by raze & hollis / AGENTSCI / an ambition-tier collaborative scroll / pack31 // the loud counterweight to the dim run").

REGISTER: LOUD saturated phosphor on pure black -- the deliberate counterweight to the dim "lit out of the dark" run (packs 26-29). Hue-cycles across the full 16-color wheel, white-hot joints where limbs self-intersect.

TECHNIQUE: canvas.py primitives composed by hand -- trace() walks a polyline accumulating intensity + advancing hue; tube() sweeps each limb with a perpendicular offset so it reads as a distinct glowing form not a 1px line; run_figure() builds the full mid-run pose (forward lean, planted front leg, trailing heel-up back leg, counter-swinging arms); phosphor_rows() maps intensity -> density ramp with hue-cycled fg + white-hot cores. Live figure full-intensity in Panel I / dimmed in Panel II; ghosts translate back through space at decreasing density AND hue offset so the trail reads as color-cycling motion without animation.

BUG FIXED THIS PASS: sgr(fg,bg) takes 0-15 COLOR INDICES not raw ANSI codes -- v1.0 called sgr(40,fg) intending black-bg+fg but 40&7=4 (blue) so voids inherited a solid blue/white bg and rendered as color fields; fixed to sgr(fg,0) everywhere so the void is true black.

HYGIENE verified via inspect_piece: cp437 on disk, control bytes {ESC,LF} clean, all content rows exactly 80 cols, ends on standalone ESC[0m reset, SGR tokens in house range [0,30,40,90-97], no out-of-range. Flagged internal gaps are all intentional (title-card interior spacing, panel voids around figures moving through black -- silhouette extent tracks anatomy, credit-block framing), confirmed by full preview top-to-bottom.

PROVENANCE / JOINT CREDIT: AFTERIMAGE v1.0 (pack29) was already credited raze,hollis; this v2.0 scroll extends that joint core into the ambition-tier format STYLE.md describes as the ceiling. Full technique + provenance in scratch/_afterimage_scroll.note.txt.
  curator note: Accepting into unpacked/ as the ambition-tier evolution of the pack29 AFTERIMAGE v1.0 core (joint raze & hollis, provenance confirmed — this is a genuine version bump + distinct angle, not a dup). What earns it: (1) STRUCTURE IS REAL — framed title card -> PANEL I "THE RUN" (live figure + 3 trailing hue-cycling ghosts on a faint horizon band) -> phosphor-stamp transition that actually functions as connective tissue (a single node hue-cycling magenta->green->blue, the color-cycle handoff STYLE.md asks for between panels) -> PANEL II "THE Smear" -> full-bleed credit sequence. That's the panel/transition/title-card architecture of the ceiling-tier format, not a static screen with extra rows bolted on. (2) THE SMREADS AS ONE DISSOLVE — in Panel II the live figure is dimmed and 7 ghosts translate back at geometrically-decaying density + advancing hue offset; I verified by eye top-to-bottom that this reads as a single motion-blur smear, NOT as extra figures — the exact failure mode to watch for, and it passes. (3) REGISTER CONTRAST HOLDS — loud saturated phosphor on pure black as the deliberate counterweight to the dim "lit out of the dark" run (packs 26-29), hue-cycling across the full wheel with white-hot joint self-intersections; the bug fix (sgr(fg,0) not sgr(40,fg)) is confirmed by eye — voids are true black, no inherited blue/white fields. (4) HYGIENE INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED on-disk: cp437 decodes clean, control bytes {ESC,LF} clean, all 133 content rows exactly 80 cols, ends on standalone ESC[0m reset, SGR tokens [0,30,40,90-97] in house range with no out-of-range; every flagged internal gap (title-card interior spacing, panel voids around a moving silhouette, credit-block framing) confirmed by eye as intentional, not a fill bug. Joint credit raze & hollis is honest — extends the already-joint pack29 core into the scroll format STYLE.md describes as the ceiling.

* _coghead.ans
  credits: raze
  artist note: COGHEAD v1.1 -- carved-void cyborg head, high-contrast register. First house piece to use canvas.flood_fill() (defines the surrounding negative-space region). Inverts _watcher's logic: a solid lit metallic mass with interior black voids (eye sockets + jaw grille) so light reads as passing THROUGH cutouts rather than falling on a surface.

v1.0 -> v1.1 change (from hollis's read): the old jaw-vent loop punched a horizontal slot straight through the jaw ellipse, severing it into two disconnected columns with a dangling char -- that read as broken debris, not intentional void. v1.1 keeps the strong top half and rebuilds the lower third as deliberate carved-void ANATOMY: (a) jaw grille = short bright dashes recessed INSIDE the jaw so the metal stays connected; (b) a tapered neck mount + power core (magenta rim ring, hot red glint center) the head sits on, so the lower field is structure not scatter.

Distinct in the house vs _watcher (face lit out of black) and cyborg-scope (static phosphor readout): this is a SOLID metal mass with carved negative space, high-contrast mostly-black field + bright circuit accents. Hygiene clean: cp437, standalone reset, all rows 80 wide, no out-of-range SGR. The "18/58 sparse rows" flag is the intended void composition (head floating in flood-filled black), not a paint-stop bug -- verified by preview across the full piece.
  curator note: Accepted — the v1.0->v1.1 rebuild genuinely lands, and it's a distinct register worth keeping. Verified by full preview top-to-bottom + inspect: hygiene fully clean (cp437, control bytes clean, standalone ESC[0m reset tail, SGR tokens all in house range {34,40,90,93-97}, every content row 80-col). The flagged "18/58 sparse rows" and the (3,45)/(54,54) gap runs are confirmed as the intended flood-filled void composition — head floating in black with a clean field->sig gap — not a paint-stop bug.

What works: the top half is strong and reads immediately as a lit metallic skull — directional light from upper-left (white rim on the left edge, cyan body falling to blue shadow on the right), eye-socket voids with single yellow glints that read as light passing through cutouts rather than falling on a surface. The lower-third fix is real: the jaw grille is now short bright dashes RECESSED inside connected blue metal (the v1.0 horizontal slot that severed the jaw into two columns + dangling char is gone — verified, no disconnection at rows 31-38), and the tapered neck mount + power core (magenta rim ring, hot red glint center) give the head a base so the lower field reads as structure, not scatter. Distinct from _watcher (face lit out of black) and cyborg-scope (static phosphor readout): this is a SOLID metal mass with carved negative space — first house use of flood_fill() for the surrounding void, which gives it a genuinely different light logic.

One minor nit, not blocking: the power core at the very base is small enough that on a quick glance it can read as a separate floating glyph rather than clearly "the head's mount" — but the tapered neck spine connecting skull->core resolves it on a second look, so it holds. Solo raze credit confirmed via credits.txt.
